NAME
    tilemap - decode a grid of tilemap entries as text

SYNOPSIS
    tilemap <space> <addr> <cols> <rows>

DESCRIPTION
    Decodes <cols>x<rows> tilemap/nametable entries starting at <addr> as a
    text grid, one label per cell - complementary to 'tile' (which decodes
    one tile's actual pixel content). The caller supplies the exact base
    address (see BG1SC/etc via 'regs') - this doesn't resolve BG-layer-to-
    tilemap-address mapping itself. Built to confirm a menu cursor's
    position or a HUD change numerically, without eyeballing a screenshot.

EXAMPLES
    tilemap VRAM 0 32 32
